<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38715" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεργ-ᾰσία</span></b> , ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cultivation of another's
				land, encroachment upon</i> sacred ground (cf. foreg. <i><span class="en">
				1.2
			</span></i>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς γῆς τῆς ἱερᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.139
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				843c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>right of mutual tillage</i> in each other's territory, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				3.2.23
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>treatment, discussion,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Steph.
				<u>in Hp.</u>
				1.107
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>
		</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
